Z||000000||GT GT 87||09-10-2001||12:15 AM||||I have a strange problem. I changed a heater core a month ago and haven't got around to putting the cover back on . The other day , when I started the car (cold) A small amount of smoke came out of the heater core into the pass. compartment. This happened on and off just a few times . Then the other , when the car was started , a Large amount came from the h-core and filled the car . The heater was not on , so what can it be ??????????||||reg||1
Z||000001||ocalafiero1||09-10-2001||01:02 AM||||What color smoke and does it have any odor? When my heater core went out on an 84 I used to have, I got some smoke out of the defrost vent on top of the dash.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||09-10-2001||02:56 PM||||GT GT 87,<BR>Sounds like a leak to me.  Check the heater core lines and connections.  Clamp connections have a way of getting loose after first being put on.  Does the smoke smell like coolant.  Coolant will leave a nasty film on the windshield that smears a lot when you try to wipe it off.  Happy hunting.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||09-10-2001||04:35 PM||||Happened to me a little while back on my 84.  I had a clogged blower motor and some debris that was stuck behind the heater core was getting hot and burning.  Anyone that remembers will most likly agree that I had an unordinary case, but might want ta check anyways.  ||||reg||1
